    "created_at": "2021-10-25T11:28:52Z",
    "updated_at": "2021-10-25T11:28:52Z",
    "body": "> I'm not sure how that helps. We know `refresh` is being used and we know it's used for redirects. We also know some percentage of users disable scripting, either directly or through an extension. Ergo, they end up with a broken experience.\r\n\r\nIf numbers are low enough of course, I still believe it would be worth pursuing: having a quick and easy way to disable meta refresh per website would make some users happy.\r\n",
    "author_association": "NONE",
