    "created_at": "2021-10-25T11:34:55Z",
    "updated_at": "2021-10-25T11:34:55Z",
    "body": "> Yes, but there's no reason to tie it to whether script runs.\r\n\r\nIt seems to me this option is the most user friendly one as it doesn't clutter settings with yet another \"specific\" option.\r\nDo you see another way for users to disable it without going too technical (.e.g `about:config`, `about:flags`, etc.) ?  ",
